<title>TOGO: Togo yr-on-yr inflation rises to 10.1 pct in May.</title>
<headline>Togo yr-on-yr inflation rises to 10.1 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>LOME 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumer prices in Lome rose by 1.5 percent in May compared with April, pushing the year-on-year inflation rate up to 10.1 percent from 9.0 percent, the government Statistics Department said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					  May		April</p>
<p>	Change on month	     +1.5 pct	 +1.0 pct</p>
<p>	Change on year		+10.1 pct	+9.0 pct</p>
<p>	Change so far in '97	+6.6 pct	 +5.1 pct</p>
<p>	Index (base 1987 = 100)   184.6	    182.1</p>
<p>The rise is due essentially to an increase in the price of cereals, fruits and other foodstuffs.</p>
<p>The government is aiming to hold inflation at 3.5 percent this year.</p>
</text>
